The src folder contains all the source code for the React application, serving as the core directory where developers write and organize their components, types, and application logic. It houses the main entry point (main.tsx) that bootstraps the React app and renders the root component (App.tsx), while also including type definitions (env.d.ts) for the Vite environment. This folder structure keeps the application's logic and components organized in one central location, making the project easy to navigate and maintain.
